<title>CANADA: Prairie grain elevator space tightens on harvest.</title>
<headline>Prairie grain elevator space tightens on harvest.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>More than two million tonnes of grain were delivered into primary elevators across the Prairies in the past week, the Canadian Wheat Board said in a statement.</p>
<p>Manitoba elevators had an average 13 percent of space remaining available, Saskatchewan had an average 22 percent of space vacant and Alberta had the most at an average 39 percent.</p>
<p>Rail hopper car unloads at Canada's West Coast reached 3,315 in the week ended Sept 22, below the target of 3,350.</p>
<p>Unloads at Thunder Bay were 2,605, up from the target 1,990 and Churchill saw 296 of the 300 rail cars allocated.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
